<?php

return [
    // Breadcrumbs
    'CSRF' => 'CSRF',
    'How to prevent CSRF vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mencegah kerentanan CSRF',

    // web-security/csrf
    'Cross-site request forgery (CSRF)' => 'Cross-site request forgery (CSRF)',
    'In this section, we\'ll explain what cross-site request forgery is, describe some examples of common CSRF vulnerabilities, and explain how to prevent CSRF attacks.' => 'Pada bagian ini dibahas apa itu cross-site request forgery (CSRF), beberapa contoh celah yang umum ditemukan, dan cara mencegah serangan CSRF.',
    'What is CSRF?' => 'Apa itu CSRF?',
    'Cross-site request forgery (also known as CSRF) is a web security vulnerability that allows an attacker to induce users to perform actions that they do not intend to perform. It allows an attacker to partly circumvent the same origin policy, which is designed to prevent different websites from interfering with each other.' => 'Cross-site request forgery (CSRF) adalah kerentanan keamanan web yang memungkinkan penyerang memaksa browser pengguna melakukan tindakan tanpa disengaja di situs target. Celah ini mengakali sebagian batasan same-origin policy yang seharusnya mencegah satu situs mencampuri situs lain.',
    'If you\'re already familiar with the basic concepts behind CSRF vulnerabilities and just want to practice exploiting them on some realistic, deliberately vulnerable targets, you can access all of the labs in this topic from the link below.' => 'Jika Anda sudah memahami konsep dasar kerentanan CSRF dan ingin langsung berlatih mengeksploitasinya pada target simulasi, akses semua lab CSRF melalui tautan berikut.',
    'What is the impact of a CSRF attack?' => 'Apa dampak serangan CSRF?',
    'In a successful CSRF attack, the attacker causes the victim user to carry out an action unintentionally. For example, this might be to change the email address on their account, to change their password, or to make a funds transfer. Depending on the nature of the action, the attacker might be able to gain full control over the user\'s account. If the compromised user has a privileged role within the application, then the attacker might be able to take full control of all the application\'s data and functionality.' => 'Pada serangan CSRF yang berhasil, korban secara tidak sadar menjalankan aksi sensitif seperti mengganti alamat email akun, mengganti kata sandi, atau mentransfer dana. Bergantung pada aksi dan hak akses korban (termasuk akun administrator), penyerang bisa mengambil alih akun hingga seluruh aplikasi.',
    'How does CSRF work?' => 'Bagaimana cara kerja CSRF?',
    'For a CSRF attack to be possible, three key conditions must be in place:' => 'Agar serangan CSRF dapat berjalan, tiga syarat utama berikut harus terpenuhi:',
    '<strong>A relevant action.</strong> There is an action within the application that the attacker has a reason to induce. This might be a privileged action (such as modifying permissions for other users) or any action on user-specific data (such as changing the user\'s own password).' => '<strong>Ada aksi penting.</strong> Tersedia aksi yang menguntungkan penyerang bila dipicu, baik tindakan administrator (seperti mengubah hak akses) maupun tindakan pada data pengguna (seperti mengubah kata sandi atau email).',
    '<strong>Cookie-based session handling.</strong> Performing the action involves issuing one or more HTTP requests, and the application relies solely on session cookies to identify the user who has made the requests. There is no other mechanism in place for tracking sessions or validating user requests.' => '<strong>Sesi hanya mengandalkan cookie.</strong> Aplikasi mengidentifikasi pengirim permintaan murni berdasarkan session cookie yang otomatis dikirim browser, tanpa verifikasi token permintaan tambahan.',
    '<strong>No unpredictable request parameters.</strong> The requests that perform the action do not contain any parameters whose values the attacker cannot determine or guess. For example, when causing a user to change their password, the function is not vulnerable if an attacker needs to know the value of the existing password.' => '<strong>Tidak ada parameter tak tertebak.</strong> Semua parameter permintaan dapat diketahui atau ditebak penyerang (misalnya fitur ganti kata sandi tidak meminta kata sandi lama).',
    'For example, suppose an application contains a function that lets the user change the email address on their account. When a user performs this action, they make an HTTP request like the following:' => 'Sebagai contoh, sebuah situs memiliki fitur ubah email akun yang mengirimkan permintaan HTTP berikut:',
    'This meets the conditions required for CSRF:' => 'Skenario tersebut memenuhi seluruh syarat CSRF karena:',
    'The action of changing the email address on a user\'s account is of interest to an attacker. Following this action, the attacker will typically be able to trigger a password reset and take full control of the user\'s account.' => 'Mengubah alamat email akun bernilai tinggi karena memungkinkan penyerang meminta reset kata sandi untuk mengambil alih akun.',
    'The application uses a session cookie to identify which user issued the request. There are no other tokens or mechanisms in place to track user sessions.' => 'Aplikasi hanya memakai session cookie untuk mengenali pengirim permintaan tanpa token pelindung tambahan.',
    'The attacker can easily determine the values of the request parameters that are needed to perform the action.' => 'Penyerang dapat dengan mudah menentukan seluruh nilai parameter yang diperlukan untuk menjalankan aksi tersebut.',
    'With these conditions in place, the attacker can construct a web page containing the following HTML:' => 'Dengan kondisi tersebut, penyerang dapat menyiapkan halaman web berisi formulir HTML yang otomatis dikirim:',
    'If a victim user visits the attacker\'s web page, the following will happen:' => 'Ketika korban mengunjungi halaman milik penyerang, rangkaian proses berikut berlangsung:',
    'The attacker\'s page will trigger an HTTP request to the vulnerable website.' => 'Halaman penyerang memicu pengiriman permintaan HTTP ke situs target yang rentan.',
    'If the user is logged in to the vulnerable website, their browser will automatically include their session cookie in the request (assuming [[A0]]SameSite cookies[[/A0]] are not being used).' => 'Jika korban sedang login di situs target, browser otomatis menyertakan session cookie milik korban selama tidak terhalang [[A0]]pembatasan cookie SameSite[[/A0]].',
    'The vulnerable website will process the request in the normal way, treat it as having been made by the victim user, and change their email address.' => 'Server target memproses permintaan seolah sah dari korban dan langsung mengganti alamat email akunnya.',
    'Although CSRF is normally described in relation to cookie-based session handling, it also arises in other contexts where the application automatically adds some user credentials to requests, such as HTTP Basic authentication and certificate-based authentication.' => 'Meski umumnya dikaitkan dengan session cookie, CSRF juga muncul pada mekanisme autentikasi lain yang otomatis dikirim browser pada setiap permintaan, seperti HTTP Basic authentication atau sertifikat klien.',
    'How to construct a CSRF attack' => 'Cara menyusun serangan CSRF',
    'Manually creating the HTML needed for a CSRF exploit can be cumbersome, particularly where the desired request contains a large number of parameters, or there are other quirks in the request. The easiest way to construct a CSRF exploit is using the [[A0]]CSRF PoC generator[[/A0]] that is built in to Burp Suite Professional:' => 'Membuat form HTML PoC secara manual bisa merepotkan bila parameternya banyak. Anda dapat menyusun [[A0]]PoC CSRF[[/A0]] dengan cepat lewat alat generator maupun template form HTML sederhana:',
    'Select a request anywhere in Burp Suite Professional that you want to test or exploit.' => 'Pilih permintaan HTTP target yang ingin diuji atau dieksploitasi.',
    'From the right-click context menu, select Engagement tools / Generate CSRF PoC.' => 'Bangkitkan kerangka form HTML (seperti tombol Generate CSRF PoC pada proksi uji).',
    'Burp Suite will generate some HTML that will trigger the selected request (minus cookies, which will be added automatically by the victim\'s browser).' => 'HTML PoC tersebut akan memicu pengiriman permintaan identik, sementara cookie sesi disematkan otomatis oleh browser korban.',
    'You can tweak various options in the CSRF PoC generator to fine-tune aspects of the attack. You might need to do this in some unusual situations to deal with quirky features of requests.' => 'Sesuaikan opsi metode, enctype, atau autosubmit pada PoC bila server membutuhkan format khusus.',
    'Copy the generated HTML into a web page, view it in a browser that is logged in to the vulnerable website, and test whether the intended request is issued successfully and the desired action occurs.' => 'Sajikan HTML tersebut dari server exploit eksternal lalu buka melalui browser yang sedang login ke target untuk memverifikasi aksi berhasil dijalankan.',
    'How to deliver a CSRF exploit' => 'Cara mengirimkan eksploitasi CSRF',
    'The delivery mechanisms for cross-site request forgery attacks are essentially the same as for reflected XSS. Typically, the attacker will place the malicious HTML onto a website that they control, and then induce victims to visit that website. This might be done by feeding the user a link to the website, via an email or social media message. Or if the attack is placed into a popular website (for example, in a user comment), they might just wait for users to visit the website.' => 'Penyaluran CSRF serupa dengan reflected XSS: penyerang menempatkan HTML berbahaya di situs kendaliannya lalu memancing korban membukanya lewat email, pesan, atau tautan, atau menyimpannya di situs pihak ketiga yang ramai dikunjungi.',
    'Note that some simple CSRF exploits employ the GET method and can be fully self-contained with a single URL on the vulnerable website. In this situation, the attacker may not need to employ an external site, and can directly feed victims a malicious URL on the vulnerable domain. In the preceding example, if the request to change email address can be performed with the GET method, then a self-contained attack would look like this:' => 'Jika aksi rentan memakai metode GET, eksploitasi bahkan cukup berupa satu URL atau tag gambar tanpa perlu halaman form eksternal:',
    'Common defences against CSRF' => 'Pertahanan umum terhadap CSRF',
    'Nowadays, successfully finding and exploiting CSRF vulnerabilities often involves bypassing anti-CSRF measures deployed by the target website, the victim\'s browser, or both. The most common defenses you\'ll encounter are as follows:' => 'Pengujian CSRF masa kini sering berkaitan dengan menembus mekanisme anti-CSRF yang dipasang aplikasi maupun browser. Tiga pertahanan utama yang paling sering dijumpai meliputi:',
    '<strong>CSRF tokens</strong> - A CSRF token is a unique, secret, and unpredictable value that is generated by the server-side application and shared with the client. When attempting to perform a sensitive action, such as submitting a form, the client must include the correct CSRF token in the request. This makes it very difficult for an attacker to construct a valid request on behalf of the victim.' => '<strong>Token CSRF.</strong> Nilai unik, rahasia, dan acak yang dibuat server untuk setiap sesi lalu wajib disertakan pada permintaan sensitif agar penyerang tidak bisa memalsukan permintaan.',
    '<strong>SameSite cookies</strong> - SameSite is a browser security mechanism that determines when a website\'s cookies are included in requests originating from other websites. As requests to perform sensitive actions typically require an authenticated session cookie, the appropriate SameSite restrictions may prevent an attacker from triggering these actions cross-site. Since 2021, Chrome enforces [[C0]] SameSite restrictions by default. As this is the proposed standard, we expect other major browsers to adopt this behavior in future.' => '<strong>Cookie SameSite.</strong> Mekanisme browser yang mengatur pengiriman cookie pada permintaan lintas situs. Browser modern berbasis Chromium menetapkan atribut bawaan [[C0]] bila tidak ditentukan secara eksplisit.',
    '<strong>Referer-based validation</strong> - Some applications make use of the HTTP Referer header to attempt to defend against CSRF attacks, normally by verifying that the request originated from the application\'s own domain. This is generally less effective than CSRF token validation.' => '<strong>Validasi berbasis header Referer.</strong> Sebagian aplikasi memeriksa apakah header HTTP Referer berasal dari domainnya sendiri, meskipun metode ini lebih rapuh dibanding token CSRF.',
    'For a more detailed description of each of these defenses, as well as how they can potentially be bypassed, check out the following materials. These include interactive labs that let you practice what you\'ve learned on realistic, deliberately vulnerable targets.' => 'Untuk mempelajari detail tiap pertahanan beserta teknik membobolnya disertai lab latihan langsung, buka topik lanjutan di bawah ini:',
    '[[S0]]LABS[[/S0]] Bypassing CSRF token validation' => '[[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]] Melewati validasi token CSRF',
    '[[S0]]LABS[[/S0]] Bypassing SameSite cookie restrictions' => '[[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]] Melewati pembatasan cookie SameSite',
    '[[S0]]LABS[[/S0]] Bypassing Referer-based CSRF defenses' => '[[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]] Melewati pertahanan CSRF berbasis Referer',
    'For details on how to properly implement these defenses in order to prevent some of these issues on your own websites, see [[A0]]How to prevent CSRF vulnerabilities[[/A0]]' => 'Untuk panduan menerapkan pertahanan ini secara tepat pada aplikasi Anda, lihat [[A0]]Cara mencegah kerentanan CSRF[[/A0]].',

    // bypassing-token-validation
    'In this section, we\'ll explain what CSRF tokens are, how they protect against CSRF attacks, and how you can potentially bypass these defenses.' => 'Bagian ini menguraikan cara kerja token CSRF dan berbagai cacat implementasi yang memungkinkan token tersebut dilewati.',
    'A CSRF token is a unique, secret, and unpredictable value that is generated by the server-side application and shared with the client. When issuing a request to perform a sensitive action, such as submitting a form, the client must include the correct CSRF token. Otherwise, the server will refuse to perform the requested action.' => 'Token CSRF adalah nilai acak rahasia per sesi yang dibagikan server kepada klien dan wajib disertakan kembali saat mengirim permintaan sensitif.',
    'A common way to share CSRF tokens with the client is to include them as a hidden parameter in an HTML form, for example:' => 'Cara paling lazim adalah menyisipkan token sebagai input tersembunyi di dalam form HTML:',
    'Submitting this form results in the following request:' => 'Saat form dikirim, permintaan HTTP-nya membawa parameter token tersebut:',
    'When implemented correctly, CSRF tokens help protect against CSRF attacks by making it difficult for an attacker to construct a valid request on behalf of the victim. As the attacker has no way of predicting the correct value for the CSRF token, they won\'t be able to include it in the malicious request.' => 'Bila diimplementasikan dengan benar, token CSRF mencegah serangan lintas situs karena penyerang tidak dapat menebak atau membaca token milik korban.',
    'CSRF tokens don\'t have to be sent as hidden parameters in a [[C0]] request. Some applications place CSRF tokens in HTTP headers, for example. The way in which tokens are transmitted has a significant impact on the security of a mechanism as a whole. For more information, see [[A0]]How to prevent CSRF vulnerabilities[[/A0]].' => 'Token CSRF tidak selalu dikirim sebagai field formulir [[C0]]; sebagian API menaruhnya di header kustom HTTP. Pelajari lebih lanjut di [[A0]]Cara mencegah kerentanan CSRF[[/A0]].',
    'Common flaws in CSRF token validation' => 'Kelemahan umum pada validasi token CSRF',
    'CSRF vulnerabilities typically arise due to flawed validation of CSRF tokens. In this section, we\'ll cover some of the most common issues that enable attackers to bypass these defenses.' => 'Banyak celah CSRF muncul bukan karena ketiadaan token, melainkan kesalahan logika saat server memvalidasi token.',
    'Some applications correctly validate the token when the request uses the POST method but skip the validation when the GET method is used.' => 'Sebagian aplikasi memvalidasi token hanya saat metode POST dipakai, namun melewatkan pengecekan ketika endpoint diakses lewat GET.',
    'In this situation, the attacker can switch to the GET method to bypass the validation and deliver a CSRF attack:' => 'Penyerang cukup mengganti metode pengiriman menjadi GET untuk melewati validasi:',
    'Some applications correctly validate the token when it is present but skip the validation if the token is omitted.' => 'Ada pula aplikasi yang memvalidasi token hanya jika parameternya dikirim, namun meloloskan permintaan bila parameter token dihapus total.',
    'In this situation, the attacker can remove the entire parameter containing the token (not just its value) to bypass the validation and deliver a CSRF attack:' => 'Dengan menghapus seluruh parameter token dari body permintaan, validasi pun terlewati:',
    'CSRF token is not tied to the user session' => 'Token CSRF tidak terikat ke sesi pengguna',
    'Some applications do not validate that the token belongs to the same session as the user who is making the request. Instead, the application maintains a global pool of tokens that it has issued and accepts any token that appears in this pool.' => 'Sebagian aplikasi hanya mengecek apakah token ada di daftar token sah secara global, tanpa mencocokkannya dengan sesi pengguna yang sedang aktif.',
    'In this situation, the attacker can log in to the application using their own account, obtain a valid token, and then feed that token to the victim user in their CSRF attack.' => 'Penyerang cukup mengambil token valid dari akunnya sendiri lalu menyematkan token tersebut ke halaman eksploitasi untuk menyerang korban.',
    'CSRF token is tied to a non-session cookie' => 'Token CSRF terikat ke cookie non-sesi',
    'In a variation on the preceding vulnerability, some applications do tie the CSRF token to a cookie, but not to the same cookie that is used to track sessions. This can easily occur when an application employs two different frameworks, one for session handling and one for CSRF protection, which are not integrated together:' => 'Variasi lain terjadi saat framework CSRF mengikat token ke cookie khusus CSRF yang terpisah dari session cookie utama aplikasi:',
    'This situation is harder to exploit but is still vulnerable. If the website contains any behavior that allows an attacker to set a cookie in a victim\'s browser, then an attack is possible. The attacker can log in to the application using their own account, obtain a valid token and associated cookie, leverage the cookie-setting behavior to place their cookie into the victim\'s browser, and feed their token to the victim in their CSRF attack.' => 'Bila terdapat celah CRLF injection atau titik penyetelan cookie di domain terkait, penyerang dapat menanam cookie pasangan miliknya ke browser korban lalu mengirim form dengan token CSRF milik penyerang.',
    'The cookie-setting behavior does not even need to exist within the same web application as the CSRF vulnerability. Any other application within the same overall DNS domain can potentially be leveraged to set cookies in the application that is being targeted, if the cookie that is controlled has suitable scope. For example, a cookie-setting function on [[C0]] could be leveraged to place a cookie that is submitted to [[C1]].' => 'Celah penyetelan cookie bahkan tidak harus berada di aplikasi yang sama; subdomain lain pada induk domain yang sama (misalnya [[C0]] terhadap [[C1]]) bisa memengaruhi cakupan cookie.',
    'CSRF token is simply duplicated in a cookie' => 'Token CSRF hanya diduplikasi di cookie',
    'In a further variation on the preceding vulnerability, some applications do not maintain any server-side record of tokens that have been issued, but instead duplicate each token within a cookie and a request parameter. When the subsequent request is validated, the application simply verifies that the token submitted in the request parameter matches the value submitted in the cookie. This is sometimes called the "double submit" defense against CSRF, and is advocated because it is simple to implement and avoids the need for any server-side state:' => 'Pada pola double submit cookie yang lemah, server tidak menyimpan state token di backend, melainkan sekadar memeriksa kecocokan antara parameter token dan nilai token di dalam cookie:',
    'In this situation, the attacker can again perform a CSRF attack if the website contains any cookie setting functionality. Here, the attacker doesn\'t need to obtain a valid token of their own. They simply invent a token (perhaps in the required format, if that is being checked), leverage the cookie-setting behavior to place their cookie into the victim\'s browser, and feed their token to the victim in their CSRF attack.' => 'Jika penyerang bisa menanam cookie di browser korban (misalnya lewat cookie injection), penyerang bahkan tidak perlu akun valid: cukup buat nilai token acak sendiri di cookie dan form sekaligus.',

    // bypassing-referer-based-defenses
    'Aside from defenses that employ CSRF tokens, some applications make use of the HTTP [[C0]] header to attempt to defend against CSRF attacks, normally by verifying that the request originated from the application\'s own domain. This approach is generally less effective and is often subject to bypasses.' => 'Selain token CSRF, beberapa aplikasi memeriksa header HTTP [[C0]] untuk memastikan permintaan berasal dari domain sendiri. Pendekatan ini umumnya lebih mudah diakali.',
    'Referer header' => 'Header Referer',
    'The HTTP Referer header (which is inadvertently misspelled in the HTTP specification) is an optional request header that contains the URL of the web page that linked to the resource that is being requested. It is generally added automatically by browsers when a user triggers an HTTP request, including by clicking a link or submitting a form. Various methods exist that allow the linking page to withhold or modify the value of the [[C0]] header. This is often done for privacy reasons.' => 'Header HTTP Referer (ejaan historis dalam spesifikasi HTTP) bersifat opsional dan dikirim browser untuk menunjukkan URL halaman asal yang memicu permintaan, namun bisa ditahan atau dipengaruhi oleh kebijakan privasi halaman pengirim.',
    'Some applications validate the [[C0]] header when it is present in requests but skip the validation if the header is omitted.' => 'Sebagian aplikasi memeriksa nilai [[C0]] hanya jika header tersebut ada, namun meloloskan permintaan ketika header Referer tidak dikirim sama sekali.',
    'In this situation, an attacker can craft their CSRF exploit in a way that causes the victim user\'s browser to drop the [[C0]] header in the resulting request. There are various ways to achieve this, but the easiest is using a META tag within the HTML page that hosts the CSRF attack:' => 'Penyerang dapat memerintahkan browser korban menyembunyikan header [[C0]] dengan menambahkan meta tag pada halaman HTML exploit:',
    'Some applications validate the [[C0]] header in a naive way that can be bypassed. For example, if the application validates that the domain in the [[C1]] starts with the expected value, then the attacker can place this as a subdomain of their own domain:' => 'Jika server hanya mengecek apakah header [[C0]] diawali nama domain target pada bagian [[C1]], penyerang dapat menggunakan subdomain bernama domain target di domain miliknya:',
    'Likewise, if the application simply validates that the [[C0]] contains its own domain name, then the attacker can place the required value elsewhere in the URL:' => 'Jika server sekadar mengecek keberadaan string nama domainnya di mana saja dalam [[C0]], penyerang cukup menaruh domain target di query string URL exploit:',
    'Although you may be able to identify this behavior using Burp, you will often find that this approach no longer works when you go to test your proof-of-concept in a browser. In an attempt to reduce the risk of sensitive data being leaked in this way, many browsers now strip the query string from the [[C0]] header by default.' => 'Perlu diperhatikan bahwa browser modern secara bawaan memotong bagian query string dari header [[C0]] saat navigasi lintas situs untuk melindungi privasi.',
    'You can override this behavior by making sure that the response containing your exploit has the [[C0]] header set (note that [[C1]] is spelled correctly in this case, just to make sure you\'re paying attention!). This ensures that the full URL will be sent, including the query string.' => 'Anda bisa memaksa browser tetap mengirim URL lengkap beserta query string dengan mengatur header respons [[C0]] pada halaman exploit (perhatikan ejaan [[C1]] dengan huruf r ganda).',

    // xss-vs-csrf
    'In this section, we\'ll explain the differences between XSS and CSRF, and discuss whether CSRF tokens can help to prevent XSS attacks.' => 'Bagian ini membandingkan XSS dan CSRF serta membahas sejauh mana token CSRF mampu meredam serangan XSS.',
    'What is the difference between XSS and CSRF?' => 'Apa perbedaan antara XSS dan CSRF?',
    '[[A0]]Cross-site scripting[[/A0]] (or XSS) allows an attacker to execute arbitrary JavaScript within the browser of a victim user.' => '[[A0]]Cross-site scripting (XSS)[[/A0]] memungkinkan penyerang mengeksekusi JavaScript sembarang di dalam browser korban pada origin aplikasi target.',
    '[[A0]]Cross-site request forgery[[/A0]] (or CSRF) allows an attacker to induce a victim user to perform actions that they do not intend to.' => '[[A0]]Cross-site request forgery (CSRF)[[/A0]] memaksa browser korban mengirim permintaan yang melakukan aksi tertentu tanpa sepengetahuannya.',
    'The consequences of XSS vulnerabilities are generally more serious than for CSRF vulnerabilities:' => 'Secara umum dampak kerentanan XSS lebih parah dibandingkan CSRF karena:',
    'CSRF often only applies to a subset of actions that a user is able to perform. Many applications implement CSRF defenses in general but overlook one or two actions that are left exposed. Conversely, a successful XSS exploit can normally induce a user to perform any action that the user is able to perform, regardless of the functionality in which the vulnerability arises.' => 'CSRF umumnya terbatas pada aksi tertentu yang proteksinya terlewat, sedangkan XSS memberi penyerang kemampuan menjalankan aksi apa saja yang diizinkan bagi korban dari fungsi mana pun.',
    'CSRF can be described as a "one-way" vulnerability, in that while an attacker can induce the victim to issue an HTTP request, they cannot retrieve the response from that request. Conversely, XSS is "two-way", in that the attacker\'s injected script can issue arbitrary requests, read the responses, and exfiltrate data to an external domain of the attacker\'s choosing.' => 'CSRF bersifat satu arah (memicu permintaan tanpa bisa membaca responsnya), sedangkan XSS bersifat dua arah karena JavaScript sisipan dapat membaca respons penuh lalu mengekspor data sensitif keluar.',
    'Some XSS attacks can indeed be prevented through effective use of CSRF tokens. Consider a simple reflected XSS vulnerability that can be trivially exploited like this:' => 'Sebagian serangan reflected XSS memang bisa terhalang token CSRF. Bayangkan URL reflected XSS sederhana berikut:',
    'Now, suppose that the vulnerable function includes a CSRF token:' => 'Jika fungsi tersebut mewajibkan token CSRF yang tervalidasi ketat:',
    'Assuming that the server properly validates the CSRF token, and rejects requests without a valid token, then the token does prevent exploitation of the XSS vulnerability. The clue here is in the name: "cross-site scripting", at least in its [[A0]]reflected[[/A0]] form, involves a cross-site request. By preventing an attacker from forging a cross-site request, the application prevents trivial exploitation of the XSS vulnerability.' => 'Karena [[A0]]reflected[[/A0]] XSS bergantung pada pengiriman permintaan dari luar, validasi token CSRF yang ketat ikut menggagalkan eksploitasi langsung melalui URL.',
    'Some important caveats arise here:' => 'Namun tetap terdapat catatan penting:',
    'If a reflected XSS vulnerability exists anywhere else on the site within a function that is not protected by a CSRF token, then that XSS can be exploited in the normal way.' => 'Jika celah reflected XSS muncul pada fitur lain yang tidak memakai token CSRF, eksploitasi tetap berjalan mulus.',
    'If an exploitable XSS vulnerability exists anywhere on a site, then the vulnerability can be leveraged to make a victim user perform actions even if those actions are themselves protected by CSRF tokens. In this situation, the attacker\'s script can request the relevant page to obtain a valid CSRF token, and then use the token to perform the protected action.' => 'Begitu ada satu celah XSS yang berhasil dijalankan di situs tersebut, skrip penyerang cukup mengambil halaman formulir untuk membaca token CSRF yang sah lalu mengirim permintaan terproteksi token atas nama korban.',
    'CSRF tokens do not protect against stored XSS vulnerabilities. If a page that is protected by a CSRF token is also the output point for a stored XSS vulnerability, then that XSS vulnerability can be exploited in the usual way, and the XSS payload will execute when a user visits the page.' => 'Token CSRF tidak melindungi dari stored XSS: begitu payload tersimpan (lewat pengguna sendiri atau celah lain) dan tampil di halaman pengunjung, skrip tetap langsung tereksekusi.',

    // bypassing-samesite-restrictions
    'SameSite is a browser security mechanism that determines when a website\'s cookies are included in requests originating from other websites. SameSite cookie restrictions provide partial protection against a variety of cross-site attacks, including CSRF, cross-site leaks, and some CORS exploits.' => 'SameSite adalah mekanisme browser untuk mengatur kapan cookie suatu situs ikut dikirim dalam permintaan yang berasal dari situs lain, sehingga memberi perlindungan parsial terhadap CSRF, cross-site leaks, dan sebagian serangan CORS.',
    'Since 2021, Chrome applies [[C0]] SameSite restrictions by default if the website that issues the cookie doesn\'t explicitly set its own restriction level. This is a proposed standard, and we expect other major browsers to adopt this behavior in the future. As a result, it\'s essential to have solid grasp of how these restrictions work, as well as how they can potentially be bypassed, in order to thoroughly test for cross-site attack vectors.' => 'Sejak 2021, Chrome menerapkan atribut [[C0]] secara bawaan bila server tidak menetapkan kebijakan SameSite secara eksplisit. Memahami cara kerja dan celah bypass-nya sangat penting saat menguji keamanan lintas situs.',
    'In this section, we\'ll first cover how the SameSite mechanism works and clarify some of the related terminology. We\'ll then look at some of the most common ways you may be able to bypass these restrictions, enabling CSRF and other cross-site attacks on websites that may initially appear secure.' => 'Bagian ini membahas definisi site vs origin, tingkat pembatasan SameSite, serta teknik umum yang dapat memicu serangan CSRF walau SameSite aktif.',
    'What is a site in the context of SameSite cookies?' => 'Apa itu site dalam konteks cookie SameSite?',
    'In the context of SameSite cookie restrictions, a site is defined as the top-level domain (TLD), usually something like [[C0]] or [[C1]], plus one additional level of the domain name. This is often referred to as the TLD+1.' => 'Dalam konteks SameSite, satu site dihitung dari top-level domain seperti [[C0]] atau [[C1]] ditambah satu level subdomain di depannya (sering disebut eTLD+1).',
    'When determining whether a request is same-site or not, the URL scheme is also taken into consideration. This means that a link from [[C0]] to [[C1]] is treated as cross-site by most browsers.' => 'Skema URL (HTTP vs HTTPS) ikut diperhitungkan dalam aturan same-site modern: tautan dari [[C0]] ke [[C1]] tetap diperlakukan sebagai cross-site oleh browser.',
    'You may come across the term "effective top-level domain" (eTLD). This is just a way of accounting for the reserved multipart suffixes that are treated as top-level domains in practice, such as [[C0]].' => 'Istilah effective top-level domain (eTLD) dipakai untuk mencakup akhiran domain bertingkat seperti [[C0]] agar tidak disalahartikan sebagai satu domain induk milik satu entitas.',
    'What\'s the difference between a site and an origin?' => 'Apa perbedaan antara site dan origin?',
    'The difference between a site and an origin is their scope; a site encompasses multiple domain names, whereas an origin only includes one. Although they\'re closely related, it\'s important not to use the terms interchangeably as conflating the two can have serious security implications.' => 'Perbedaan utamanya ada pada cakupan: satu site mencakup beberapa subdomain sekaligus, sedangkan satu origin hanya berlaku untuk satu pasangan skema, host, dan port persis sama.',
    'Two URLs are considered to have the same origin if they share the exact same scheme, domain name, and port. Although note that the port is often inferred from the scheme.' => 'Dua URL dikatakan same-origin hanya apabila skema, nama domain (termasuk subdomain), dan port-nya identik.',
    'As you can see from this example, the term "site" is much less specific as it only accounts for the scheme and last part of the domain name. Crucially, this means that a cross-origin request can still be same-site, but not the other way around.' => 'Karena definisi site lebih longgar, sebuah permintaan cross-origin antar subdomain tetap berstatus same-site, sedangkan sebaliknya permintaan cross-site pasti cross-origin.',
    '<strong>Request from</strong>' => '<strong>Permintaan dari</strong>',
    '<strong>Request to</strong>' => '<strong>Permintaan ke</strong>',
    '<strong>Same-site?</strong>' => '<strong>Same-site?</strong>',
    '<strong>Same-origin?</strong>' => '<strong>Same-origin?</strong>',
    'Yes' => 'Ya',
    'No: mismatched domain name' => 'Tidak: nama domain berbeda',
    'No: mismatched port' => 'Tidak: port berbeda',
    'No: mismatched eTLD' => 'Tidak: eTLD berbeda',
    'No: mismatched scheme' => 'Tidak: skema berbeda',
    'This is an important distinction as it means that any vulnerability enabling arbitrary JavaScript execution can be abused to bypass site-based defenses on other domains belonging to the same site. We\'ll see an example of this in one of the labs later.' => 'Pembedaan ini penting karena celah pada satu subdomain (seperti XSS atau open redirect) dapat dipakai untuk melewati proteksi berbasis same-site pada subdomain saudara lainnya.',
    'How does SameSite work?' => 'Bagaimana cara kerja SameSite?',
    'Before the SameSite mechanism was introduced, browsers sent cookies in every request to the domain that issued them, even if the request was triggered by an unrelated third-party website. SameSite works by enabling browsers and website owners to limit which cross-site requests, if any, should include specific cookies. This can help to reduce users\' exposure to CSRF attacks, which induce the victim\'s browser to issue a request that triggers a harmful action on the vulnerable website. As these requests typically require a cookie associated with the victim\'s authenticated session, the attack will fail if the browser doesn\'t include this.' => 'Sebelum ada SameSite, cookie otomatis ikut terkirim di setiap permintaan lintas situs. SameSite membatasi pengiriman cookie pada permintaan lintas situs sesuai tingkat kebijakannya sehingga membantu meredam CSRF.',
    'All major browsers currently support the following SameSite restriction levels:' => 'Semua browser utama mendukung tiga tingkat pembatasan SameSite berikut:',
    'Developers can manually configure a restriction level for each cookie they set, giving them more control over when these cookies are used. To do this, they just have to include the [[C0]] attribute in the [[C1]] response header, along with their preferred value:' => 'Pengembang mengatur kebijakan dengan menambahkan atribut [[C0]] pada header respons [[C1]]:',
    'Although this offers some protection against CSRF attacks, none of these restrictions provide guaranteed immunity, as we\'ll demonstrate using deliberately vulnerable, interactive labs later in this section.' => 'Walau membantu pertahanan, tidak satu pun level SameSite memberikan kekebalan mutlak bila masih ada celah lain di situs atau subdomain terkait.',
    'If the website issuing the cookie doesn\'t explicitly set a [[C0]] attribute, Chrome automatically applies [[C1]] restrictions by default. This means that the cookie is only sent in cross-site requests that meet specific criteria, even though the developers never configured this behavior. As this is a proposed new standard, we expect other major browsers to adopt this behavior in future.' => 'Jika server tidak menyertakan atribut [[C0]], browser Chromium menerapkan [[C1]] secara otomatis pada cookie baru.',
    'Strict' => 'Strict',
    'If a cookie is set with the [[C0]] attribute, browsers will not send it in any cross-site requests. In simple terms, this means that if the target site for the request does not match the site currently shown in the browser\'s address bar, it will not include the cookie.' => 'Dengan [[C0]], cookie tidak akan pernah dikirim pada permintaan cross-site apa pun, termasuk saat pengguna mengklik tautan biasa dari situs lain.',
    'This is recommended when setting cookies that enable the bearer to modify data or perform other sensitive actions, such as accessing specific pages that are only available to authenticated users.' => 'Kebijakan ini disarankan untuk cookie sesi yang mengizinkan aksi sensitif atau pengubahan data.',
    'Although this is the most secure option, it can negatively impact the user experience in cases where cross-site functionality is desirable.' => 'Meski paling ketat, level Strict bisa mengganggu navigasi bila pengguna sering datang dari tautan eksternal dalam keadaan sudah login.',
    'Lax' => 'Lax',
    '[[C0]] SameSite restrictions mean that browsers will send the cookie in cross-site requests, but only if both of the following conditions are met:' => 'Pada kebijakan [[C0]], browser tetap mengirim cookie lintas situs hanya apabila kedua syarat berikut terpenuhi:',
    'The request uses the [[C0]] method.' => 'Permintaan memakai metode [[C0]].',
    'The request resulted from a top-level navigation by the user, such as clicking on a link.' => 'Permintaan dipicu oleh navigasi tingkat atas (top-level navigation) seperti mengklik tautan atau pengalihan lokasi halaman.',
    'This means that the cookie is not included in cross-site [[C0]] requests, for example. As [[C1]] requests are generally used to perform actions that modify data or state (at least according to best practice), they are much more likely to be the target of CSRF attacks.' => 'Cookie tidak dikirim dalam permintaan [[C0]] lintas situs (yang semestinya dipakai untuk operasi pengubah data, berbeda dengan [[C1]]).',
    'Likewise, the cookie is not included in background requests, such as those initiated by scripts, iframes, or references to images and other resources.' => 'Cookie juga tidak disertakan pada permintaan latar belakang seperti fetch/XHR, iframe tersembunyi, atau tag gambar.',
    'None' => 'None',
    'If a cookie is set with the [[C0]] attribute, this effectively disables SameSite restrictions altogether, regardless of the browser. As a result, browsers will send this cookie in all requests to the site that issued it, even those that were triggered by completely unrelated third-party sites.' => 'Dengan [[C0]], seluruh batasan SameSite dinonaktifkan sehingga cookie ikut dikirim di semua permintaan lintas situs termasuk form POST dari situs pihak ketiga.',
    'With the exception of Chrome, this is the default behavior used by major browsers if no [[C0]] attribute is provided when setting the cookie.' => 'Beberapa browser lama memakai perilaku ini sebagai bawaan jika atribut [[C0]] tidak dituliskan.',
    'There are legitimate reasons for disabling SameSite, such as when the cookie is intended to be used from a third-party context and doesn\'t grant the bearer access to any sensitive data or functionality. Tracking cookies are a typical example.' => 'Pengaturan ini dipakai untuk cookie pihak ketiga yang memang sah berjalan lintas situs (misalnya widget tertanam atau cookie pelacak non-autentikasi).',
    'If you encounter a cookie set with [[C0]] or with no explicit restrictions, it\'s worth investigating whether it\'s of any use. When the "Lax-by-default" behavior was first adopted by Chrome, this had the side-effect of breaking a lot of existing web functionality. As a quick workaround, some websites have opted to simply disable SameSite restrictions on all cookies, including potentially sensitive ones.' => 'Bila menemukan cookie dengan [[C0]], periksa apakah ada endpoint pengubah state yang dapat diserang lewat CSRF klasik.',
    'When setting a cookie with [[C0]], the website must also include the [[C1]] attribute, which ensures that the cookie is only sent in encrypted messages over HTTPS. Otherwise, browsers will reject the cookie and it won\'t be set.' => 'Cookie bertanda [[C0]] wajib disertai atribut [[C1]] dan disetel melalui HTTPS agar diterima oleh browser modern.',
    'Bypassing SameSite Lax restrictions using GET requests' => 'Melewati pembatasan SameSite Lax dengan permintaan GET',
    'In practice, servers aren\'t always fussy about whether they receive a [[C0]] or [[C1]] request to a given endpoint, even those that are expecting a form submission. If they also use [[C2]] restrictions for their session cookies, either explicitly or due to the browser default, you may still be able to perform a CSRF attack by eliciting a [[C3]] request from the victim\'s browser.' => 'Banyak server menerima baik metode [[C0]] maupun [[C1]] pada endpoint yang sama. Jika cookie sesi berstatus [[C2]], penyerang cukup memicu navigasi [[C3]] lintas situs agar cookie tetap ikut terkirim.',
    'As long as the request involves a top-level navigation, the browser will still include the victim\'s session cookie. The following is one of the simplest approaches to launching such an attack:' => 'Karena navigasi langsung mengarahkan tab browser, cookie berstatus Lax otomatis disertakan lewat pengalihan skrip sederhana berikut:',
    'Even if an ordinary [[C0]] request isn\'t allowed, some frameworks provide ways of overriding the method specified in the request line. For example, Symfony supports the [[C1]] parameter in forms, which takes precedence over the normal method for routing purposes:' => 'Bahkan jika [[C0]] murni ditolak, beberapa framework menyediakan fitur method override seperti parameter [[C1]] di dalam form GET:',
    'Other frameworks support a variety of similar parameters.' => 'Sejumlah framework lain memiliki parameter serupa untuk menimpa metode HTTP.',
    'Bypassing SameSite restrictions using on-site gadgets' => 'Melewati pembatasan SameSite memakai gadget di dalam situs',
    'If a cookie is set with the [[C0]] attribute, browsers won\'t include it in any cross-site requests. You may be able to get around this limitation if you can find a gadget that results in a secondary request within the same site.' => 'Meski cookie bernilai [[C0]], Anda masih bisa melewatinya jika menemukan gadget di situs target (seperti pengalihan sisi klien) yang memicu permintaan kedua berasal dari dalam situs itu sendiri.',
    'One possible gadget is a client-side redirect that dynamically constructs the redirection target using attacker-controllable input like URL parameters. For some examples, see our materials on [[A0]]DOM-based open redirection[[/A0]].' => 'Contoh gadget paling sering adalah pengalihan sisi klien yang membaca URL tujuan dari parameter tanpa validasi; lihat materi [[A0]]DOM-based open redirection[[/A0]].',
    'As far as browsers are concerned, these client-side redirects aren\'t really redirects at all; the resulting request is just treated as an ordinary, standalone request. Most importantly, this is a same-site request and, as such, will include all cookies related to the site, regardless of any restrictions that are in place.' => 'Bagi browser, navigasi lanjutan dari JavaScript di halaman situs target diperlakukan sebagai permintaan baru berstatus same-site sehingga cookie SameSite Strict pun ikut terbawa.',
    'If you can manipulate this gadget to elicit a malicious secondary request, this can enable you to bypass any SameSite cookie restrictions completely.' => 'Jika gadget pengalihan tersebut bisa diarahkan ke endpoint aksi dengan parameter berbahaya, pembatasan SameSite dapat dilewati sepenuhnya.',
    'Note that the equivalent attack is not possible with server-side redirects. In this case, browsers recognize that the request to follow the redirect resulted from a cross-site request initially, so they still apply the appropriate cookie restrictions.' => 'Berbeda dengan itu, redirect HTTP sisi server (302) tetap melacak asal rantai permintaan lintas situs sehingga cookie Strict tetap ditahan browser.',
    'Bypassing SameSite restrictions via vulnerable sibling domains' => 'Melewati pembatasan SameSite melalui subdomain saudara yang rentan',
    'Whether you\'re testing someone else\'s website or trying to secure your own, it\'s essential to keep in mind that a request can still be same-site even if it\'s issued cross-origin.' => 'Ingatlah bahwa permintaan antar subdomain berbeda tetap dihitung sebagai same-site walaupun berstatus cross-origin.',
    'Make sure you thoroughly audit all of the available attack surface, including any sibling domains. In particular, vulnerabilities that enable you to elicit an arbitrary secondary request, such as XSS, can compromise site-based defenses completely, exposing all of the site\'s domains to cross-site attacks.' => 'Audit juga seluruh subdomain pada site induk yang sama, karena celah seperti XSS di salah satu subdomain sudah cukup untuk mengirim permintaan same-site ke subdomain utama.',
    'In addition to classic CSRF, don\'t forget that if the target website supports WebSockets, this functionality might be vulnerable to cross-site WebSocket hijacking (CSWSH), which is essentially just a CSRF attack targeting a WebSocket handshake. For more details, see our topic on [[A0]]WebSocket vulnerabilities[[/A0]].' => 'Selain CSRF HTTP standar, periksa koneksi WebSocket terhadap cross-site WebSocket hijacking (CSWSH); pelajari selengkapnya di topik [[A0]]kerentanan WebSocket[[/A0]].',

    // preventing
    'In this section, we\'ll provide some high-level guidance on how you can protect your own websites from the kinds of vulnerabilities we\'ve demonstrated in our CSRF labs.' => 'Bagian ini menyajikan panduan tingkat tinggi untuk melindungi aplikasi web dari seluruh teknik serangan CSRF di atas.',
    'Use CSRF tokens' => 'Gunakan token CSRF',
    'The most robust way to defend against CSRF attacks is to include a CSRF token within relevant requests. The token must meet the following criteria:' => 'Pertahanan paling andal terhadap CSRF adalah menyertakan token CSRF pada setiap permintaan sensitif dengan syarat berikut:',
    'Unpredictable with high entropy, as for session tokens in general.' => 'Tidak dapat ditebak dan memiliki entropi tinggi seperti halnya token sesi.',
    'Tied to the user\'s session.' => 'Terikat erat dengan sesi pengguna yang bersangkutan.',
    'Strictly validated in every case before the relevant action is executed.' => 'Selalu divalidasi secara ketat pada setiap metode dan format sebelum aksi dijalankan.',
    'How should CSRF tokens be generated?' => 'Bagaimana token CSRF harus dibuat?',
    'CSRF tokens should contain significant entropy and be strongly unpredictable, with the same properties as session tokens in general.' => 'Token CSRF harus dibangkitkan dengan tingkat keacakan kriptografis yang tinggi.',
    'You should use a cryptographically secure pseudo-random number generator (CSPRNG), seeded with the timestamp when it was created plus a static secret.' => 'Gunakan pembangkit bilangan acak aman kriptografis (CSPRNG) dengan panjang byte yang memadai.',
    'If you need further assurance beyond the strength of the CSPRNG, you can generate individual tokens by concatenating its output with some user-specific entropy and take a strong hash of the whole structure. This presents an additional barrier to an attacker who attempts to analyze the tokens based on a sample that are issued to them.' => 'Bila diperlukan lapisan tambahan, gabungkan keluaran CSPRNG dengan data sesi spesifik pengguna lalu ambil hash kriptografisnya agar pola token makin sulit dianalisis.',
    'How should CSRF tokens be transmitted?' => 'Bagaimana token CSRF harus dikirimkan?',
    'CSRF tokens should be treated as secrets and handled in a secure manner throughout their lifecycle. An approach that is normally effective is to transmit the token to the client within a hidden field of an HTML form that is submitted using the POST method. The token will then be included as a request parameter when the form is submitted:' => 'Perlakukan token CSRF sebagai rahasia sesi. Cara yang paling umum adalah menyematkannya sebagai input tersembunyi di dalam form POST:',
    'For additional safety, the field containing the CSRF token should be placed as early as possible within the HTML document, ideally before any non-hidden input fields and before any locations where user-controllable data is embedded within the HTML. This mitigates against various techniques in which an attacker can use crafted data to manipulate the HTML document and capture parts of its contents.' => 'Tempatkan field tersembunyi token sedini mungkin di dalam form (sebelum data masukan pengguna tampil di DOM) guna meredam teknik pencurian isi halaman seperti dangling markup.',
    'An alternative approach, of placing the token into the URL query string, is somewhat less safe because the query string:' => 'Menaruh token CSRF di query string URL kurang aman karena query string:',
    'Is logged in various locations on the client and server side;' => 'Tercatat di log server, riwayat browser, serta proksi perantara;',
    'Is liable to be transmitted to third parties within the HTTP Referer header; and' => 'Berisiko bocor ke situs pihak ketiga lewat header Referer; serta',
    'can be displayed on-screen within the user\'s browser.' => 'Tampak jelas di bilah alamat browser pengguna.',
    'Some applications transmit CSRF tokens within a custom request header. This presents a further defense against an attacker who manages to predict or capture another user\'s token, because browsers do not normally allow custom headers to be sent cross-domain. However, the approach limits the application to making CSRF-protected requests using XHR (as opposed to HTML forms) and might be deemed over-complicated for many situations.' => 'Mengirim token di header HTTP kustom lewat XHR/fetch juga efektif karena dibatasi oleh CORS dan pre-flight lintas domain, meski hanya berlaku pada permintaan asinkron.',
    'CSRF tokens should not be transmitted within cookies.' => 'Hindari mengandalkan pengiriman token CSRF semata di dalam cookie.',
    'How should CSRF tokens be validated?' => 'Bagaimana token CSRF harus divalidasi?',
    'When a CSRF token is generated, it should be stored server-side within the user\'s session data. When a subsequent request is received that requires validation, the server-side application should verify that the request includes a token which matches the value that was stored in the user\'s session. This validation must be performed regardless of the HTTP method or content type of the request. If the request does not contain any token at all, it should be rejected in the same way as when an invalid token is present.' => 'Simpan token di data sesi server lalu verifikasi bahwa nilai token pada permintaan cocok persis dengan token sesi aktif, tanpa memandang metode HTTP atau Content-Type, dan tolak segera bila token kosong atau tidak dikirim.',
    'Use Strict SameSite cookie restrictions' => 'Terapkan pembatasan cookie SameSite Strict',
    'In addition to implementing robust CSRF token validation, we recommend explicitly setting your own SameSite restrictions with each cookie you issue. By doing so, you can control exactly which contexts the cookie will be used in, regardless of the browser.' => 'Selain validasi token CSRF, tetapkan atribut SameSite secara eksplisit pada setiap cookie agar perlakuannya konsisten di seluruh browser.',
    'Even if all browsers eventually adopt the "Lax-by-default" policy, this isn\'t suitable for every cookie and can be more easily bypassed than [[C0]] restrictions. In the meantime, the inconsistency between different browsers also means that only a subset of your users will benefit from any SameSite protections at all.' => 'Mengandalkan bawaan Lax dari browser belum cukup melindungi seluruh endpoint (khususnya rute GET yang mengubah state) dibanding aturan [[C0]] yang konsisten.',
    'Ideally, you should use the [[C0]] policy by default, then lower this to [[C1]] only if you have a good reason to do so. Never disable SameSite restrictions with [[C2]] unless you\'re fully aware of the security implications.' => 'Gunakan [[C0]] secara default, turunkan ke [[C1]] hanya bila benar-benar dibutuhkan untuk navigasi eksternal, dan hindari [[C2]] pada cookie sesi.',
    'Be wary of cross-origin, same-site attacks' => 'Waspadai serangan cross-origin tetapi same-site',
    'Although properly configured SameSite restrictions provide good protection from cross-site attacks, it\'s vital to understand that they are completely powerless against cross-origin, same-site attacks.' => 'Ingatlah bahwa SameSite tidak melindungi terhadap serangan yang berasal dari subdomain berbeda di dalam site induk yang sama.',
    'If possible, we recommend isolating insecure content, such as user-uploaded files, on a separate site from any sensitive functionality or data. When testing a site, be sure to thoroughly audit all of the available attack surface belonging to the same site, including any of its sibling domains.' => 'Pisahkan konten unggahan pengguna atau fitur berisiko pada site induk terpisah (berbeda eTLD+1) dan selalu audit seluruh subdomain saudara di lingkup organisasi Anda.',
];
